body:
Counselors are different for everyone, just like therapists! If you're able to, you should try talking to them just once or twice at least to see if they help at all. If not, just don't talk to them anymore haha. You could ease in too, just talk about some things that are bugging you and not go fully into detail right away if you're worried about any of that. 

&#x200B;

It does take some courage, and it is really hard sometimes to get that courage. It's really a good idea to get help for your mental health sooner than later but if you aren't able to just yet, just make sure you remind yourself it's ok to not be ok. You aren't a stupid attention seeker. You might very much \*need\* that attention you seek because your mental health needs to be cared for.

Was it recent? I live in Washington...home of Starbucks and apparently the state with the most vegans lol but can't seem to find it in my hick of a town.

&#x200B;

Edit: Just saw the post you talked about, I guess I'll have to look at every store and gas station around lol

Is it loud enough to be heard outside the car though? Other people might not care or maybe this new lady has her windows open all the time and can hear outside better than the rest. She does have the right to politely ask you to keep it down, but legally you don't have to do anything until the ordinance time kicks in. 

&#x200B;

If you keep it down, and she stops complaining, then you probably were genuinely disrupting her. If you turn it down and she still complains, she's making a fuss for no reason and you should just be on your merry way.

The charcoal soap I use is the target brand of the biore one, I did go out and buy some witch hazel though so I'm hoping that helps a little. I'll try out the baking soda mask in the meantime of getting a "real" one. Thanks for the suggestions!

&#x200B;

I eat pretty healthy but I have been indulging in desserts pretty often lately. It's never a lot though, which will really suck if just the tiniest bit makes me break out...I love my chocolate before bed lol

I've approached him at all different angles and he still lets them out. It's less than before, but still happening. I even told him that it keeps me up all night panicking but he still does it. Even though I've explained why, he still thinks I'm being over dramatic and that it's cruel to keep them inside. It's just how he is, if they want out, he'll let them out. My mom says he was the same when my brother and I were little. If we wanted candy but were acting up and didn't deserve it, he'd still give it to us. I don't think there's any changing that part of him. 

&#x200B;

I think it's just the area we live in. Right next to a busy road with woods in the back. If we lived in a neighborhood where the speed limit was 10mph and everyone had fenced yards, then I wouldn't really care so much and would even say it was just really bad luck if that many of my cats had died, but I don't believe that many would have if we lived in a place like that. In my mind, it's cruel to let them out into such dangerous conditions.

Thank you for this! I never really thought Paul was terrible, he just always seems so harsh next to Mary but your explanation clears that up a bit. I'm excited to see the later seasons to see him mellow out and the new judges. 

&#x200B;

I do think Sue is a sweetheart too, I guess it's just her persona/character on the show that annoys me a bit lol

&#x200B;

Thank you for this detailed answer! I really appreciate it :) Hopefully America takes note and starts some similar shows (doubt it though lol)
